desc:MakeGain Tap (stereo) — copies channels 1/2 into 3/4 as the pre-chain dry tap
//tags: utility gain-staging makegain
//author: auto-make-gain (AGPLv3, https://github.com/…/auto-make-gain)
//
// PURPOSE (FR §10.1/§10.7, A2): MakeGain nulls the loudness delta its
// host chain introduces. It needs the PRE-CHAIN dry signal on its aux
// bus. This FX makes the wiring trivial for ONE track:
//
//   chain order:  [MakeGain Tap] … any chain FX … [MakeGain  ← last]
//
// The Tap copies the track's own input into lanes 3/4 at chain entry.
// Ordinary stereo FX do not write lanes 3/4, so those lanes ride
// untouched through the whole chain = still the dry signal. MakeGain
// (its own 4-pin build) reads lanes 3/4 as the aux. No sends, no second
// track.
//
// Reaper notes: writing lanes 3/4 auto-raises the track's channel count.
// On a MONO track use "MakeGainTap Mono" instead (copies 1 → 2).
// Misroute warning (documented): feeding the stereo aux ONE dry channel
// reads −6 dB and overcompensates — hard-panned aux content is legal,
// so the plugin will not detect/correct that for you.

in_pin:audio L
in_pin:audio R
out_pin:audio L
out_pin:audio R
out_pin:dry L
out_pin:dry R

@sample
spl3 = spl0;
spl4 = spl1;
